                    <msContents>
                        <summary>An early illustrated copy of the Assemblies of Ḥarīrī.</summary>
                        <msItem xml:id="manuscript_14377_item_1">
                            <title xml:lang="ar-Latn-x-lc" key="work_21224">Maqāmāt
                                al-Ḥarīrī</title>
                            <title xml:lang="ar" type="alt">مقامات الحريري</title>
                            <title xml:lang="en" type="alt">The Assemblies of Hārīrī</title>
                            <author key="person_9907600">
                                <persName xml:lang="en">Ḥarīrī,
                                    1054-1122</persName>
                                <persName xml:lang="ar"> ابو محمد القاسم بن علي بن محمد
                                    الحريري</persName>
                            </author>
                            <textLang mainLang="ar">Arabic</textLang>
                            <note>
                                <p>The manuscripts contains the 50 maqāmāhs with the usual Preface
                                    and Epilogue (where the author gives his name as <quote>ابو محمد
                                        القاسم بن علي بن محمد الحريري</quote>. It does not contain
                                    however the Risālahs appended in some copies (e.g. John Rylands
                                    Library, Arabic MS 664).</p>
                                <p/>
                            </note>
                            <incipit>قال الشيخ الامام ابو محمد القسم بن على بن محمد بن عثمان الحريري
                                رض الله عنه اللهم</incipit>
                        </msItem>
                    </msContents>
                    <physDesc>
                        <objectDesc form="codex">
                            <supportDesc material="paper">
                                <support>
                                    <material>paper</material>
                                </support>
                                <extent>172 folios (no flyleaf). <dimensions type="leaf" unit="mm">
                                        <height>337</height>
                                        <width>154</width>
                                    </dimensions>
                                </extent>
                                <foliation>One leaf is missing between folios 134 and
                                    135.</foliation>
                                <collation>
                                    <catchwords>Catchword on every verso on the mount, added by a
                                        later hand.</catchwords>
                                </collation>
                                <condition><p>Part of folio 89 is lost.</p>
                                    <p>A leaf is missing between folios 134 and 135, and the
                                        contents were written in the lower margin, but a part of
                                        that was lost in the binding..</p></condition>
                            </supportDesc>
                            <layoutDesc>
                                <layout columns="1 2" ruledLines="15">
                                    <p>The leaves are all inlaid except folios 2 and 46 which are
                                        more recent.</p>
                                    <p>The inlaid parts of folios 14 and 33 are of a different
                                        paper, and the lines longer.</p>
                                    <p>Red rulings, broad margins.</p>
                                    <p><dimensions type="written" unit="mm">
                                            <height>249</height>
                                            <width>173</width>
                                        </dimensions></p></layout>
                            </layoutDesc>
                        </objectDesc>
                        <handDesc>
                            <handNote scope="major" script="naskh" medium="ink">Bold, clear Naskh of
                                ca. the beginning of the 13th century CE or not more than a hundred
                                years after Ḥarīrī's death. Fully vocalised.</handNote>
                            <handNote scope="minor" script="kufi">The maqāmah headings were
                                originally in illuminated kūfi script. </handNote>
                            <handNote scope="minor" script="kufi">Naskh script of maqāmah headings,
                                of the 17th century. </handNote>
                        </handDesc>
                        <decoDesc>
                            <decoNote>131 coloured illustrations: 109 of large size, occupying
                                roughly half of the page, and 32 smaller.</decoNote>
                            <decoNote><locus from="89b" to="90a">Folios 89b-90a</locus>: miniature
                                occupies both pages of the opening.</decoNote>
                            <decoNote>Illuminated headings; originally in kūfi (e.g. folios 4a,
                                29a). A 17th-century hand covered the kūfi titles thin slips bearing
                                titles in illuminated Naskh (e.g. folios 6b, 9a, 11a). In places,
                                this later slip with the Naskh title has been partially come off and
                                parts of the original kūfi title are visible (e.g. folios <locus
                                    from="23a">23a</locus> and <locus from="26a"
                                >26a</locus>).</decoNote>
                        </decoDesc>
                        <additions>
                            <p>Folios 2 and 46 are later additions.</p>
                            <p>Folios 157-171 seems to be later additions: paper whiter, writing
                                closer, vowels fewer, style different. The illustrations in this
                                part are the 32 smaller ones. The notes of the manuscript having
                                been read are on these leaves.</p>
                            <p>Folio 2a (new title page): imperfect citation from
                            Zamakhshari.</p></additions>
                        <bindingDesc>
                            <binding calendar="#Gregorian" notBefore="1501" notAfter="1600">
                                <p>Oriental binding, gold-tooled with central mandorlas on both
                                    covers and paste-downs; probably of the 16th century.</p>
                                <p><dimensions type="cover" unit="mm">
                                        <height>338</height>
                                        <width>255</width>
                                        <depth>50</depth>
                                    </dimensions></p>
                            </binding>
                        </bindingDesc>
                    </physDesc>
                    <history>
                        <origin>Produced in the <origDate calendar="#Gregorian" notBefore="1201"
                                notAfter="1225">early 13th century</origDate>.</origin>
                        <provenance>
                            <p>Ownership inscription by the maulawi (<quote>حثمت ودود</quote>) of
                                the 17th century.</p>
                        </provenance>
                        <provenance>
                            <p>Inscribed by reader on <locus from="170b">folio 170b</locus>:
                                    <quote>ونظر فى هذا الكتاب احمد ... فى الحوران فى سنه...</quote>.
                                Mingana deciphers the name as <quote>احمد الاسيهي</quote>. </p>
                        </provenance>
                        <provenance><p>Several more inscriptions on folios 172a and 172b, to be
                                deciphered.</p></provenance>
                        <provenance>
                            <p>Purchase note: <quote>Empsit Damasci Theodorus Preston Coll. S.S.
                                    Trin. Cant. Soc. 1847 A.D." <persName key="37282724 " role="fmo"
                                        >Theodore Preston</persName> is the author of the abridged
                                    translation of Harīrī in the <title>Oriental Translations
                                        Fund</title> series.</quote>
                            </p>
                        </provenance>
                        <provenance>
                            <p>
                                <name source="#viaf" key="97751058" role="fmo">
                                    <persName type="display">Alexander Lindsay, 25th Earl of
                                        Crawford (1812-1880), book collector and writer on
                                        art</persName>
                                    <persName type="standard">Crawford, Alexander Crawford Lindsay,
                                        1812-1880</persName>
                                </name>
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                <name source="#viaf" key="9985420" role="fmo">
                                    <persName type="display">James Ludovic Lindsay, 26th Earl of
                                        Crawford (1847-1913), astronomer and book
                                        collector</persName>
                                    <persName type="standard">Crawford, James Ludovic Lindsay, Earl
                                        of, 1847-1913</persName>
                                </name>
                            </p>
                            <p>Formerly in the Crawford Library (Bibliotheca Lindesiana) at Haigh
                                Hall, Lancashire, which was formed and developed by Alexander and
                                James Ludovic Lindsay.</p>
                            <p>His bookplate on <locus from="172b">172b</locus>: <quote>Bibliotheca
                                    Lindesiana E/3</quote>.</p>
                            <p>Crawford's handwritten label on <locus from="172b">172b</locus>:
                                        <quote><del>Additional</del> MSS. Arabic No. <del>197</del>
                                    <del>666</del> 677 المقامات الحريري Al-Maqámatu l-Harírí</quote>
                            </p>
                        </provenance>
                        <provenance>
                            <p>
                                <name key="person_f6379" role="fmo">
                                    <persName type="display">Enriqueta Rylands (1843-1908),
